<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <share-target android:targetClass="org.telegram.ui.LaunchActivity">
        <data android:mimeType="*/*" />
        <category android:name="org.telegram.messenger.SHORTCUT_SHARE" />
    </share-target>

    <!--
        NovaGram: the Assistant App Actions upstream declares here are removed.

        Each <capability> registered a tg:// deep link with the system's assistant:
        actions.intent.GET_THING -> tg://search{?query}, CREATE_CALL -> tg://call
        {?format,name,phone}, plus GET_ACCOUNT, GET_BARCODE and GET_CALL. Advertising
        them means a spoken or typed request naming a person to call, or a phrase to
        search for in this client, is parsed by the assistant - so the contact name
        and the query reach it before this application sees anything, and they are
        handled under whatever retention that assistant applies. This build ships
        without Google Services at all, so nothing was gained in exchange.

        The <share-target> above stays: it is the system share sheet and the direct
        share row, both of which are driven by the app's own ShortcutManager
        publishing and stay under the client's control.
    -->
</shortcuts>
